  "description": "Non material amendment to planning permission ref. 12/AP/1092 dated 27th March 2013 (Outline application for: Redevelopment to provide a mixed use development comprising a number of buildings ranging between 13.13m (AOD) and 104.8m (AOD) in height with capacity for between 160,579sqm GEA (min) and 254,000sqm GEA (max) residential floorspace together with retail (Class A1-A5), business (Class B1), leisure and community (Class D2 and D1), energy centre (sui generis) uses. New landscaping, park and public realm, car parking, means of access and other associated works). \rThe amendment proposes to adjust the minimum requirement for each non-residential land use as follows: revision of the minimum floor areas within Table 4.2 of the Development Specification to reduce the minimum area of Class A retail space, increase the minimum areas of Classes B1, D1 and D2 uses, and reduce the minimum area of parking, plant, servicing and storage. These result in the same total combined minimum GEA floorspace for Class A, B1, D1 and D2 uses as approved. \r",
